            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0545" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Belgium/173: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Belgium</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-03T17:00:00-05:00">December 3, 1935—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Your despatch No. 641, November 18. Your efforts and those of Mr. Sussdorff
                    to obtain cooperation in suppression of smuggling are greatly appreciated.</p>
                <p>Question of approaching other exporting nations receiving consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
